Below are the attractions that are **currently topping the “Our top picks” (trending) list** for Milan on the travel‑partner platform, plus a few extra crowd‑pleasers that families love.  I’ve grouped them by type, added a quick “why it’s hot” note, and included practical tips (tickets, best times, kid‑friendly activities, nearby food stops) so you can plan a smooth family itinerary.

| # | Attraction | Category | Why It’s Trending (2024‑2025) | Family‑Friendly Tips |
|---|------------|----------|------------------------------|----------------------|
| **1** | **Duomo di Milano** | Landmark | The rooftop glass‑walk with 360° city views is a TikTok‑favorite; a nightly “light‑show” on the façade has gone viral. | • **Buy the combined ticket** (cathedral + rooftop) on the official site to skip the line. <br>• Elevator takes you straight to the terraces – kids love the quick ascent. <br>• Bring a light jacket; the rooftop can be breezy. |
| **2** | **Leonardo da Vinci’s “The Last Supper” (Cenacolo Vinciano)** | Tour / Landmark | Limited‑time “behind‑the‑scenes” virtual tour has reignited interest; tickets sell out fast, making it a coveted bucket‑list item. | • **Book 2‑3 weeks ahead** via the official booking page. <br>• Choose the **early‑morning slot (8 am)** for fewer crowds and calmer kids. <br>• The venue is wheelchair‑accessible; bring a stroller‑friendly bag. |
| **3** | **Leonardo da Vinci Museum of Science & Technology** | Museum | The museum’s new “Science Lab for Kids” (hands‑on experiments, robotics demos) is a top‑rated activity on TripAdvisor and a bestseller on the platform. | • Allocate **2 hours**; the kids’ area is compact and easy to navigate. <br>• Free entry for children under 12 (check the ticket page). <br>• Bring a sketchbook – the interactive exhibits inspire doodling. |
| **4** | **Torre Branca** (Panoramic Tower) | Landmark / Viewpoint | A short‑rise tower offering sweeping city views; the “sunset‑photo‑spot” has become a popular Instagram reel. | • Buy tickets **online** for a skip‑the‑line entry. <br>• The elevator is stroller‑friendly. <br>• Combine with a walk through **Parco Sempione** (playground & picnic area). |
| **5** | **Self‑Guided Walking Tour – “Milan’s Best‑Kept Secrets”** | Tour (App‑Based) | A downloadable audio‑guide that uncovers hidden courtyards, street‑art, and local cafés; the app’s “gamified scavenger‑hunt” is trending with families. | • Download the app **before you arrive** (available on iOS/Android). <br>• The tour is **self‑paced** – perfect for kids who need breaks. <br>• Pack a water bottle; the route is ~2 km and mostly flat. |
| **6** | **Food‑Focused Tours – “Discover Milano by Food” & “Taste Milano Food Experience”** | Food / Tour | Street‑food stalls, gelato‑making workshops, and a “pizza‑making class for kids (6+)” have become viral on TikTok. | • Reserve a **morning slot** (10 am‑12 pm) to avoid lunch crowds. <br>• Most tours provide **high‑chairs** and kid‑friendly portions. |
| **7** | **Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II** | Shopping Arcade | The glass‑dome, luxury boutiques, and the “touch‑the‑bull” good‑luck tradition are Instagram staples. | • Quick gelato stop at **Camparino** or **Pasticceria Marchesi** inside the arcade. <br>• Stroller‑friendly; the floor is flat and well‑lit. |
| **8** | **Navigli District (Canal Area)** | Nightlife / Walk | Evening “light‑up” boat tours with live acoustic music are a favorite for families on Instagram reels. | • Take a **30‑minute boat ride** at sunset; kids love the illuminated bridges. <br>• Finish with gelato at **Gelateria “La Dolce Vita”** on the canal side. |
| **9** | **Pinacoteca di Brera** | Museum / Art | The “Renaissance Remix” AR exhibition (see the original colors via a phone app) has driven a surge in family visits. | • Use the **Kids’ Trail** map (available at the desk) for a fun scavenger‑hunt. <br>• Café offers child‑size pastries and high‑chairs. |
| **10** | **Sforza Castle (Castello Sforzesco)** | Landmark / Outdoor | A new **interactive history‑quest** app (QR‑based scavenger hunt) is boosting family footfall. | • Rent a **family audio guide** (multiple languages). <br>• After the castle, relax in **Parco Sempione** – it has a new adventure playground (rope bridges, mini‑zip line). |

